  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 339 AM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nAn anomalously strong ridge remains over the Four Corners\nregion, but the Bermuda High is beginning to retrograde from the\nAtlantic to the Gulf Coast. As it treks westward this week, it\nwill come to be the dominant feature in our synoptic pattern and\nbecome a stronger limiting factor for rain chances. High PWAT\nvalues near 2 inches will persist in the region through midweek,\nso increasing heat will push our daily heat index values more\nreliably over 105 degrees across the area tomorrow onward. Showers\nand thunderstorms will bring spotty relief from the heat. Drier\nair will wrap from the Gulf and southwestern US as the ridge\nbecomes more prevalent, and PWAT values will fall closer to 1.5\ninches by next Friday and Saturday. The increasing temps may be a\nlittle offset by the decreasing humidity, but suffice it to say\nthat heat stress will be a concern as we push solidly into mid\nAugust. /NF/",
